# .env.example
#
# This repo has no full env-var reference file yet — most existing vars
# (DATABASE_URL, ADMIN_MIGRATIONS_SECRET, CRON_SECRET, MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY,
# ...) are provisioned outside of dotenv files today. This file currently
# documents only the Web Push vars added by WS1 Task 9
# (docs/superpowers/sdd/task-9-brief.md); extend it as more vars gain a
# documented .env.local convention.
#
# VAPID (Voluntary Application Server Identification) keys identify this
# server to push services (FCM, Mozilla's autopush, ...) when sending Web
# Push notifications (lib/push/send.ts). Generate a real keypair for local
# dev with:
#
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#
# or programmatically via the package's generateVAPIDKeys(). Put the
# generated values in your own .env.local (git-ignored) — never commit a
# real keypair. VAPID_SUBJECT must be a `mailto:` contact the push services
# can use to reach the sender if a key is misused.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:ops@example.com
